# Text size — default to `<p>` / base

Body copy, text inside content components, and common UI text **inherit the app base size** (`text-base` on `body`, same as an unstyled `<p>`).

Unstyled `<p>` defaults to **`text-muted-foreground`** (`@apply` in `@layer base`). Use `text-foreground` only when the paragraph should read as primary emphasis. Do not re-add `text-muted-foreground` on `<p>` by default.

Do **not** set `text-sm` / etc. on layout shells or content wrappers (Card, Dialog content, Sheet content, TabsContent, page sections) just to “match the UI.”

Only add a size utility when deliberately denser or larger:

- ✅ `<p>Supporting copy</p>` — muted + base by default
- ✅ `<p className="text-sm">Ordered Aug 5</p>` — intentional denser meta (still muted)
- ✅ `<p className="text-foreground">Pending request from Alex Chen</p>` — intentional primary
- ✅ Button and TabsTrigger use `text-base` (same as a regular `<p>`); Badge uses `text-sm` (on the primitives; regular weight by inheritance)
- ✅ Input and other control chrome may define their own size tokens
- ❌ `<Card className="text-sm">` or Dialog/Sheet roots forcing `text-sm` for all children
- ❌ `<p className="text-muted-foreground">…</p>` when muted is already the default

See `design.md` → Typography → Default size.
